    "findings": [
      {
        "kind": "info",
        "person_id": "",
        "description": "Directory https://cec.fiu.edu/about/directory/ re-downloaded 2026-11-25T02:29:22Z; bytes identical to the earlier run (373,550 bytes, sha256 e55da126...). 307 cards, all in static HTML, no pagination. The card for Anis Allagui and Stavros Koulouridis still shows name only (no title or department tag), so their roster status rests on their profiles."
      },
      {
        "kind": "info",
        "person_id": "",
        "description": "Of the 307 cards, 52 carry an Electrical & Computer Engineering tag or title. These match brief.people exactly apart from Allagui and Koulouridis, which are untagged (see their decisions). Nine cards carry several tags; the ECE-professorial multi-tag entries are Pulugurtha, Rahman and Uluagac, and the other six are advisors or staff."
      },
      {
        "kind": "info",
        "person_id": "",
        "description": "All 27 untagged directory cards were re-fetched (27/27 HTTP 200) and their profile headers checked. 22 are non-ECE staff or administration. Maria C. Benincasa mentions a past ECE coordinator role but her current role is Office of the Dean. Laura Gimenez (Sr. Administrative Assistant, Office of the Dean), Ines Triay (Executive Director, Applied Research Center) and Ximena Gallegos (Executive Director of Development) have no ECE role. Ana Posadas is \"Program Coordinator | Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering\" (staff, not faculty, not in brief; excluded as academic_professional if added, so not an omission)."
      },
      {
        "kind": "info",
        "person_id": "",
        "description": "No omissions found: every ECE faculty member identified on the directory or the official profiles is in brief.people. Gallo: no directory card or profile in this roster has the surname Gallo; closest are Emily Gallego (card tagged Moss School of Construction only) and Ximena Gallegos (no ECE text). The older ECE page cited in the task was not supplied and is not in brief.supporting_urls, so that reported listing could not be checked."
      },
      {
        "kind": "info",
        "person_id": "",
        "description": "Jannette Perez (https://cec.fiu.edu/about/directory/profiles/jannette-perez.html, retrieved 2026-11-25T02:30:06Z): header \"Adjunct Faculty | Multidisciplinary Engineering and Computing Education, Systems and Management Department\"; no ECE affiliation; excluded as adjunct and not an omission."
      },
      {
        "kind": "decision",
        "person_id": "person_625d82e0065353bf82e1",
        "description": "Included as courtesy, per the user rule (courtesy only with an explicit courtesy ECE appointment and a professorial rank on an official page). Quoted from the official profile: header \"Associate Professor | Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering\"; biography \"He also holds a position of Courtesy Professor in Florida International University ... since 2020 (Dept. of Mechanical & Materials Engineering 2020-2023, and Dept. of Electrical & Computer Engineering since 2023)\". Outcome if the courtesy statement were read as FIU-wide rather than ECE-specific: category becomes regular (the header still gives an ECE Associate Professor), and the count is unchanged. The ECE start year is not used as effective_from_json."
      },
      {
        "kind": "decision",
        "person_id": "person_c457b185e1a6580da11b",
        "description": "Excluded as affiliate per the user rule. Profile header: \"Courtesy Faculty | Electrical & Computer Engineering\"; no professorial rank appears on the profile, the directory card (name only), or any page linked from the profile or the directory. Would change to included (courtesy) only if an official page gives a professorial rank for him. Searches outside the two linked official pages were not made."
      },
      {
        "kind": "decision",
        "person_id": "person_d5cc461314fb5bd1a55c",
        "description": "Included as joint_secondary on the directory ECE tag plus Associate Professor rank. The official profile header lists only the Knight Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences and does not mention ECE. Policy source precedence gives the official designated roster priority, so the roster tag decides. If the ECE tag is treated as non-authoritative, the outcome changes to excluded (cs_only)."
      },
      {
        "kind": "decision",
        "person_id": "person_826df7c7fad551ac8d15",
        "description": "Included as joint_secondary: directory and profile both list Biomedical Engineering and Electrical & Computer Engineering. Regular-vs-courtesy subtype not stated, so not guessed. Count unchanged either way."
      },
